== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Charred Warrior|Aggressive creature strategies#Charred Warrior}}

=== Swing ===
A vertical sword slash that creates a 3-meter 115-degree arc in front (150 [[Damage types#Slash|Slash]] damage). It can be used every 3 seconds when within 1.6 meters of a player.

=== Thrust ===
A forward stab that extends in a 3-meter line which arcs slightly by 10 degrees (160 [[Damage types#Pierce|Pierce]] damage). This attack can be used every 3 seconds when within 1.6 meters of a player.

=== Feint ===
Shares the same windup as the swing, but they will suddenly pause before shifting stances to attack with a different slash that hits in a 3-meter 77.3-degree vertical arc (130 [[Damage types#Slash|Slash]] damage). It can be used every 8 seconds when within 1.6 meters of a player. There is practically no difference between the animation for this attack and that of the regular swing<ref group="Note">The timing difference between the regular swing and the feint is approximately 0.57 seconds.</ref>; there is more than enough time to react and parry again, but the attack will catch rolling players unless completely moving out of their range.

=== Thrust feint ===
Shares the same windup as the thrust, but they will suddenly pause before attacking with an upward swing from their current stance (160 [[Damage types#Pierce|Pierce]] damage). This attack creates a vertical arc that is 3 meters long and spans 60 degrees. It can be used every 3 seconds when within 1.6 meters of a player. Similar to the regular feint, there is practically no difference between the animation for this attack and that of the regular thrust<ref group="Note">The timing difference between the thrust and the feint is approximately 0.631 seconds.</ref>; there is more than enough time to react and parry again, but the attack will catch rolling players unless completely moving out of their range.

=== Notes ===
<references group="Note"/>

==Tips==
* It is difficult to predict whether an attack is a feint or not, to parry the attack effectively the player can try to [[parry]] the first part of the attack, if no parry animation is played the attack is a feint, then the player can quickly release and hold the block button again to parry the second part.
* Feint attacks can be identified by their unique sounds. Both feint attacks share the same set of sounds.
